 "notes": [
  "National I-O: industry-by-industry coefficients A = D·B from the summary Make and Use tables (industry-technology assumption), aggregated to model sectors before the product. Scrap/used goods and noncomparable imports are dropped as leakages.",
  "Domestic coefficients: each row of A scaled by (1 - national import share of that commodity), import share = imports / (intermediate use + domestic final use).",
  "County output = BEA county GDP by industry x national (output / value added) for that sector. BEA folds owner-occupied housing into county real estate GDP; it is split off in national HS:(ORE+532RL) value-added proportions.",
  "BEA county GDP cells suppressed \"(D)\" are filled with county jobs x national value added per job.",
  "City share of each sector = LODES city workplace jobs / county workplace jobs in that NAICS sector. LODES has no public/private split, so the GOV share is the public-administration (CNS20) share — an approximation for public schools and hospitals."
 ]
}
